        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0723" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/301.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 232.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-08-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that, by an
                    executive order dated August 29, 1911, Mr. Zemurray is empowered to negotiate in
                    the United States, for the Government of Honduras, a loan of $500,000 in gold,
                    the proceeds thereof to be used to defray the expenses of the recent war, which
                    the Provisional Government considers itself bound to liquidate in accordance
                    with the bases of peace signed at the Conference in Puerto Cortes in May
                    last.</p>
                <p>Mr. Zemurray left Tegucigalpa immediately thereafter, for Puerto Cortes and
                    Ceiba. Thence he intends to go direct to Washington to acquaint the Department
                    with the terms of the matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Butler Wright</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
